{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00131",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.94,
      "end_seconds": 4.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Ready for you, doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.0,
      "end_seconds": 8.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.06,
      "end_seconds": 16.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out. We came because of a mole that has changed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.81,
      "end_seconds": 20.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.47,
      "end_seconds": 27.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "Hm. It was either the end of last month or earlier than that. I couldn't tell you the date."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.54,
      "end_seconds": 32.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.56,
      "end_seconds": 38.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a bit of itching on it as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.94,
      "end_seconds": 44.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 44.79,
      "end_seconds": 49.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.96,
      "end_seconds": 57.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "I was getting to that! The bit of itching on it? That's been for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.82,
      "end_seconds": 64.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Right, have you had a mole that has changed before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.61,
      "end_seconds": 68.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "A bit, last year. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.98,
      "end_seconds": 86.56,
      "duration_seconds": 16.58,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.28,
      "end_seconds": 91.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.42,
      "end_seconds": 95.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Have you had any history of sunburn or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.52,
      "end_seconds": 106.87,
      "duration_seconds": 10.35,
      "text": "No, no history of sunburn, no weight loss. I did have it bled once at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.35,
      "end_seconds": 115.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Any history of skin cancer, pain or lumps in the armpit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.58,
      "end_seconds": 120.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.35,
      "end_seconds": 125.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.8,
      "end_seconds": 127.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.09,
      "end_seconds": 132.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.03,
      "end_seconds": 135.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 137.07,
      "end_seconds": 144.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Respiratory rate 18, SpO2 98 percent on room air, heart rate 81. Blood pressure 110 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.96,
      "end_seconds": 150.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "So, thanks. What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.56,
      "end_seconds": 163.18,
      "duration_seconds": 11.62,
      "text": "Just my thyroid operated on, a long time ago. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.65,
      "end_seconds": 166.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.87,
      "end_seconds": 181.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.85,
      "text": "Spironolactone. I take it 25 milligrams, once a day for my heart. It's the not knowing that gets to me. I take apixaban, 5 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 182.98,
      "end_seconds": 190.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the apixaban was 10 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.19,
      "end_seconds": 194.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.27,
      "end_seconds": 203.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. I'm on iron tablets, once a day for my blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.79,
      "end_seconds": 211.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a little pink tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.01,
      "end_seconds": 214.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.49,
      "end_seconds": 223.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.09,
      "text": "For my cholesterol, I believe. My son sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.41,
      "end_seconds": 228.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.21,
      "end_seconds": 239.98,
      "duration_seconds": 9.77,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.5,
      "end_seconds": 244.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.39,
      "end_seconds": 246.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.18,
      "end_seconds": 251.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.44,
      "end_seconds": 255.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "My brother has asthma. Yeah, my father had kidney stones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.5,
      "end_seconds": 262.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.51,
      "end_seconds": 265.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "I have heart failure, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.9,
      "end_seconds": 267.6,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.01,
      "end_seconds": 269.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "I've got an irregular heartbeat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.35,
      "end_seconds": 271.31,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.8,
      "end_seconds": 278.88,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "Low haemoglobin, for nearly five years. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.98,
      "end_seconds": 280.68,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.11,
      "end_seconds": 285.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "High cholesterol, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.82,
      "end_seconds": 296.11,
      "duration_seconds": 9.29,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known heart failure. We'll keep that in mind today. Okay, an irregular heartbeat, that's already on your record. Good to know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.17,
      "end_seconds": 301.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.8,
      "end_seconds": 304.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Can you lie back for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.74,
      "end_seconds": 322.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "I can't feel any glands in the armpit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.77,
      "end_seconds": 324.47,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.99,
      "end_seconds": 327.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.25,
      "end_seconds": 345.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "It's about eight millimetres, with an uneven border and two shades of brown."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.11,
      "end_seconds": 375.6,
      "duration_seconds": 24.49,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like a pigmented lesion that needs to be looked at more closely. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. It could also be a seborrhoeic keratosis, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.41,
      "end_seconds": 379.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.75,
      "end_seconds": 396.51,
      "duration_seconds": 16.76,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a pigmented lesion that needs to be looked at more closely do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a mole that has changed, and no history of sunburn or pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.56,
      "end_seconds": 398.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.47,
      "end_seconds": 407.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Let's get a skin biopsy, for changing mole. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 409.33,
      "end_seconds": 413.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "We have a slot Monday at 3:30 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.95,
      "end_seconds": 417.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Monday, that works for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 417.97,
      "end_seconds": 443.09,
      "duration_seconds": 25.12,
      "text": "I'm going to order a dermoscopy, for changing mole. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. Please use sunscreen and cover up in the midday sun, and check your skin once a month. We'll refer you to a dermatologist. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 445.9,
      "end_seconds": 447.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 448.77,
      "end_seconds": 455.17,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 455.5,
      "end_seconds": 456.2,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 457.6,
      "end_seconds": 462.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the biopsy results. Alright, good. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 464.14,
      "end_seconds": 467.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Right, no, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 467.8,
      "end_seconds": 468.57,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}